      "content": "Your hands are no longer tools but the very evidence of a life fully lived, and that is far more precious than any future utility you can imagine. The emptiness you feel is simply the quiet aftermath of a lifetime of giving, a space now open for you to finally rest without the weight of expectation. You are not taking up space; you are occupying the only place that mattered, and that is enough.",
